# Host-specific config written by scripts/setup.sh. Never personal values in
# source -- see superbird.conf.example and INSTALL.md.
#
# Deliberately NOT named ".env": this file holds a device serial and a couple
# of LAN hostnames, not credentials, and ".env" both overstates that and is
# blanket-blocked by some agent/tooling sandboxes -- which makes a config file
# your own tools cannot read or maintain. Same KEY=VALUE format either way;
# systemd's EnvironmentFile= does not care what it is called.
/superbird.conf

# Also ignored: the conventional dotenv name. This project does NOT use it,
# but ignoring it is cheap insurance -- dropping the rule when the config was
# renamed is exactly how a real local config got swept into a commit by a
# bulk `git add` here on 2026-08-15. Ignore both names; stage explicitly.
/.env
/.env.*

node_modules/

# Build output. `npm run build` in device/ emits both; neither was ignored,
# so the first thing a fresh clone does after following INSTALL.md was leave
# untracked build artifacts sitting in `git status`.
device/dist/
device/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
services/panel-gateway-token.txt
